melyar (0.0.3.2a-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Local music import feature: .m3u, .pls, .json, .csv format support added
  * Import button added to bottom toolbar with file dialog
  * Enhanced ImportOverlay with format type descriptions
  * GitHub: feat/plugins branch with all import functionality
  * TypeScript and Rust compilation verified

 -- MAKHMUDJON MURODOV <mahmudjonmurodov@mail.ru>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 19:18:00 +0300

melyar (0.0.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Third release: the InnerTube configuration is read from the web client at
    runtime and several client identities are tried in turn, so a version that
    has quietly gone stale can no longer break playback. yt-dlp is optional
    now; streams resolve without it.
  * The interface meets WCAG AA contrast in both themes, and the accent tints
    work on Qt 6.4, which has no color-mix() and is what Ubuntu 24.04 ships.
    The full screen player, which stays dark in both themes, was writing the
    light theme's grey text on its own surface at 2.87:1.
  * Continuous integration audits the interface at three window sizes in both
    themes and holds memory to a budget of 400 MB, measured at 318 MB.

 -- MAKHMUDJON MURODOV <mahmudjonmurodov@mail.ru>  Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:15:53 +0300

melyar (0.0.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Second release: settings that persist, thirteen languages, library import
    from another service and a Debian package.
  * Native YouTube Music client for Linux, built on a Rust core with a Qt 6
    shell and a React interface.

